WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:17.086
Jason hadn't put down his video game all day.

2
00:00:17.087 --> 00:00:21.600
He was too busy trying to reach level five of Dragon Lands.

3
00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:26.112
Right now he was battling dragons on the way to Kids Central.

4
00:00:26.113 --> 00:00:29.934
He was about to reach the final battle of level four when . . .

5
00:00:29.935 --> 00:00:33.644
Smack! He walked right into Nina.

6
00:00:33.645 --> 00:00:39.850
"Watch where you're going!" she cried.

7
00:00:39.851 --> 00:00:44.052
"Sorry, Nina. I'm trying to finish—" he began.

8
00:00:44.053 --> 00:00:51.283
"It's time to put the video game away," Miss Shelly reminded Jason.

9
00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:54.497
"For today's activity, you'll need a book.

10
00:00:54.498 --> 00:00:56.739
Grab a dictionary!"

11
00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:02.705
Bobby groaned. "A dictionary? Why?"

12
00:01:02.706 --> 00:01:06.679
Miss Shelly held up a thick piece of paper with her name on it.

13
00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.073
"We're making name poem bookmarks."

14
00:01:10.074 --> 00:01:13.653
Jason tucked his game into his backpack.

15
00:01:13.654 --> 00:01:16.112
"What's a name poem?"

16
00:01:16.113 --> 00:01:21.136
"It's a poem that uses the letters in your name," Miss Shelly explained.

17
00:01:21.137 --> 00:01:23.230
"My first name is Marie.

18
00:01:23.231 --> 00:01:27.222
So the first word in my poem will begin with M.

19
00:01:27.223 --> 00:01:29.829
The next line will begin with A.

20
00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:35.094
Every line should describe you."

21
00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:37.793
"Magical," Ethan said.

22
00:01:37.794 --> 00:01:41.118
"What's that, Ethan?" Miss Shelly asked.

23
00:01:41.119 --> 00:01:44.594
"That could be the first word in your poem," he said.

24
00:01:44.595 --> 00:01:48.039
"Because like magic, you make things fun."

25
00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.780
"What are the dictionaries for?" asked Nina.

26
00:01:51.781 --> 00:01:55.122
"Dictionaries help when you can't think of a word."

27
00:01:55.123 --> 00:01:58.871
Miss Shelly handed out blank bookmarks.

28
00:01:58.872 --> 00:02:01.745
"Write your name poem on these when you're done.

29
00:02:01.746 --> 00:02:04.988
Then you can use them as bookmarks."

30
00:02:04.989 --> 00:02:08.675
Jason scribbled his name on a piece of paper.

31
00:02:08.676 --> 00:02:12.105
J wasn't the easiest letter to start with.

32
00:02:12.106 --> 00:02:15.462
"Jolly?" he thought.

33
00:02:15.463 --> 00:02:18.107
"Sounds too much like Santa Claus."

34
00:02:18.108 --> 00:02:21.779
Next was A. He sighed.

35
00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.434
He was awful at writing poems.

36
00:02:24.435 --> 00:02:29.968
"Awful! 'Awful' begins with A!"

37
00:02:29.969 --> 00:02:34.106
He stared at the S and yawned.

38
00:02:34.107 --> 00:02:36.499
"Sleepy!" he thought.

39
00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.163
That was easy.

40
00:02:38.164 --> 00:02:39.934
Then there was O.

41
00:02:39.935 --> 00:02:44.335
Jason opened the dictionary to the first page of Oo.

42
00:02:44.336 --> 00:02:49.839
There were mostly words he didn't know, like "obsolete" and "obscure."

43
00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:53.108
He looked through all the letter O words.

44
00:02:53.109 --> 00:02:58.684
He decided that "odd" was the only O word that might work.

45
00:02:58.685 --> 00:03:03.734
When everyone was finished, Miss Shelly called on Ethan to read his poem.

46
00:03:03.735 --> 00:03:10.543
"Excellent surfer, Totally cool, Helpful, Adventurous, and New," he read.

47
00:03:10.544 --> 00:03:14.308
"Because I'm still new to Sunny Dale."

48
00:03:14.309 --> 00:03:16.518
Jason was next.

49
00:03:16.519 --> 00:03:21.101
"Jumpy, Awful, Sleepy, Odd, Nut," he read.

50
00:03:21.102 --> 00:03:24.397
"Nut?" Izzie asked, confused.

51
00:03:24.398 --> 00:03:29.087
"I saw that 'nut' can mean a strange or silly person," he said.

52
00:03:29.088 --> 00:03:34.608
"Jason, are you sure those words describe you?" Miss Shelly asked.

53
00:03:34.609 --> 00:03:39.312
"They're not bad words, but I could think of nicer words."

54
00:03:39.313 --> 00:03:44.910
"Yeah, like J for 'Jigsaw puzzle wizard!'" Bobby said.

55
00:03:44.911 --> 00:03:47.972
"You're great at puzzles."

56
00:03:47.973 --> 00:03:51.660
"And A for 'awesome,'" Nina said.

57
00:03:51.661 --> 00:03:56.086
"S for 'super,'" Izzie added. "Or 'sweet.'"

58
00:03:56.087 --> 00:04:03.180
"O for the 'only' person who can reach level four in the Dragon Lands video game!" Ethan said.

59
00:04:03.181 --> 00:04:07.313
Jason smiled. "You guys are good at this!"

60
00:04:07.314 --> 00:04:10.475
He began writing his new poem.

61
00:04:10.476 --> 00:04:14.419
"But keep N for 'nut,'" Bobby said, grinning.

62
00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:23.129
"Because you can be pretty strange."
